+# spectrace
+
+Specs you can change your mind about.
+
+spectrace turns a natural-language interview into specs — requirements, design,
+tasks — where every decision has an ID and a revision, and every task records exactly
+what it changed. When a decision changes, it lists the tasks, files, lines and tests
+that implemented the old one and turns them into cleanup tasks, so nothing from the
+old approach is left behind. Any agent executes the tasks; there is no orchestrator.
+
+> Status: pre-release. Not yet verified end to end (`planning/specs/006-e2e-verification`).
+
+## Install
+
+Claude Code and GitHub Copilot CLI, from the plugin marketplace:
+
+```sh
+claude plugin marketplace add SebassContreras/spectrace --sparse .claude-plugin skills && claude plugin install spectrace@spectrace
+copilot plugin marketplace add SebassContreras/spectrace && copilot plugin install spectrace@spectrace
+```
+
+Any harness that reads `.agents/skills/` (OpenCode, Codex, Cursor, Copilot, Antigravity):
+
+```sh
+curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SebassContreras/spectrace/main/install.sh | bash
+```
+
+```powershell
+irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SebassContreras/spectrace/main/install.ps1 | iex
+```
+
+Needs git and Python 3.9+ in the project. Nothing else.
+
+## Three skills
+
+| Skill | What it does |
+|---|---|
+| `start` | Interviews you one question at a time and writes `planning/` — product, architecture (A items), roadmap, each spec's requirements (R items) — plus `.spectrace/trace.py` and the task protocol in `AGENTS.md`. |
+| `plan` | Closes a spec's design (D items, each naming the R items it implements) and breaks it into tasks, each declaring what it `covers:`. |
+| `change` | Revises or retires decisions, records why, and turns everything that implemented the old one into cleanup tasks — redo by default, refactor only with a written reason. |
+
+## Executing tasks
+
+Tell any agent to execute the specs. The protocol in `AGENTS.md` has it run:
+
+```sh
+python3 .spectrace/trace.py status          # next task
+python3 .spectrace/trace.py start 002/T004  # snapshot before editing
+python3 .spectrace/trace.py done 002/T004   # record exactly what changed
+python3 .spectrace/trace.py check           # must pass before finishing
+```
+
+`start` and `done` snapshot the working tree without committing or touching the
+staging area, so each task's diff is exact even when several tasks share one commit
+or none. The diff is kept in `.spectrace/changes/` and summarized on the task.
+
+## Changing direction
+
+```
+- ~~D1@1 (implements R1): Sessions live in localStorage.~~ retired 2026-10-12 → D3
+- D3@1 (implements R1): Sessions live in an httpOnly cookie.
+```
+
+```
+$ python3 .spectrace/trace.py impact 001/D1
+- 001/T001 [agent] [done] Session store
+    src/store.ts: 14/14 added lines still present
+```
+
+Every finished task that covered `D1@1` is now *suspect*; the spec can't read as done
+until a task retires it. The format is defined once, in
+[`skills/start/assets/format.md`](skills/start/assets/format.md).
+
+## Develop
+
+```sh
+python3 -m unittest discover -s tests
+python3 skills/start/assets/trace.py check
+```
+
+This repo is planned with spectrace itself: see `planning/` and `AGENTS.md`.
